      "question": "What is a status flag?",
      "solution_html": "<ul class='list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 my-1 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Answer</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>A status flag is a bit in the flag register used to indicate the result or condition of</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>an arithmetic or logical operation, such as zero, carry, sign, or overflow.</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Definition <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(1 mark)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Example/condition mention <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(1 mark)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Fax machine</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>(Other valid examples may be accepted.)</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>1 mark each example</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>(Answer any 4 questions – Each carries 5 marks)</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Faster instruction execution</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Decode</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>CPI (Cycles Per Instruction)</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>CPU Execution Time</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>CPU Time=Instruction Count × CPI × Clock Cycle Time</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>OR</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Performance ∝ Clock FrequencyCPI</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Clock Frequency</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Number of clock cycles per second</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Higher frequency → faster execution</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>CPI</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Average cycles needed per instruction</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Lower CPI → better performance</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Impact</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>High clock frequency improves speed</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Low CPI reduces execution time</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Performance depends on balance of both</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Example</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Processor A</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>3 GHz, CPI = 2</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Processor B</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>2 GHz, CPI = 1</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Processor B may perform similarly because of lower CPI.</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Factors affecting CPI</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Instruction set complexity</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Pipeline efficiency</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Cache performance</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Conclusion</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Efficient CPU design aims for high clock frequency and low CPI to improve overall</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>performance.</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Marking Scheme (15 Marks)</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Definition of CPI <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(2 marks)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Clock frequency explanation <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(3 marks)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Formula <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(2 marks)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Performance relationship <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(3 marks)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Example <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(2 marks)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Conclusion/factors <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(3 marks)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm 