      "question": "Define Flash memory.",
      "solution_html": "<ul class='list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 my-1 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Answer</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Flash memory is a non-volatile semiconductor memory that can be electrically</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>erased and reprogrammed.</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Non-volatile memory <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(1 mark)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Electrically erasable/reprogrammable <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(1 mark)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Suitable for RISC processors</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Execute</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Dispatch unit sends instructions to available execution units</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Set-Associative Mapping</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Cache divided into sets.</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Address Structure</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>| T ag | Set | Word |</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Features</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Combination of direct and associative mapping</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Better performance</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Comparison</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Direct → simple</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Associative → flexible</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Set-associative → balanced</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Marking Scheme</li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Direct mapping explanation + structure <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(5 marks)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Associative mapping explanation + structure <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(5 marks)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>Set-associative explanation + structure <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(5 marks)</span></li><li class='leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300'>CPU saves program state</li></ul>",
